    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d346">

                <pb facs="0792" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">961.53/10–1554: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 346<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Republic of China
                            (Rankin) to the
                            Department of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d346-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-15T17:00:00+09:00">October 15, 1954—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>275. Department’s 228.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d346-f2"/> Instructions re Soviet
                    tanker in reference telegram carried out today in conversation with acting
                    Foreign Minister. He will consult other members of government and give us
                    reply.</p>
                <p>Shen said no further efforts being made obtain defections
                    among Soviet crew and defectors to date (16 or 19) being rescreened by <pb
                        facs="0793" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/> Chinese to verify genuineness. French
                    Embassy has instructions from Paris to interview crew members and will be
                    allowed do so in day or two.</p>
                <p>Minister noted Chinese Government had not yet formally acceded to request for
                    asylum in case of Soviet crew members and would prefer not do so until United
                    States position clear re willingness permit entry US.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d346-f3"/> Uncertainty on this point he said was having bad effect
                    on morale of defectors particularly since apparent reversal US position re
                    admission <hi rendition="#italic">Praca</hi> and <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gottwald</hi> defectors who now giving
                    trouble.</p>
                <p>I urged US actions not be used as basis for delay in reaching decisions re <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tuapse</hi> and crew, particularly since we were not
                    party to dispute.</p>
                <p>Shen anticipated early resolution in case of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tuapse</hi> crew, but could say nothing more about
                    disposal of ship. (See third [<hi rendition="#italic">fourth</hi>] paragraph my
                    September 13 letter to McConaughy.)<anchor n="4" xml:id="d346-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Rankin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d346-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d346-f1-content">
                <p>Also sent to Paris, USUN at New York, Moscow, and Warsaw.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d346-f2" n="2" xml:id="d346-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see <ref target="#d329-f5">footnote 5, Document 329</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d346-f3" n="3" xml:id="d346-f3-content">
                <p>Attorney General Brownell announced on Oct. 22 that the
                    United States would admit 22 Polish seamen from the crews of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Praca</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">President
                            Gottwald</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d346-f4" n="4" xml:id="d346-f4-content">
                <p><ref target="#d294">Document 294</ref>. The paragraph citation was corrected by
                    hand on the source text.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
